Thanks for the precise info - I would like to point out one small mistake: 
the probability that a wand is a WoW is 0.005, not 0.05 (as you assumed).
Thus your numbers are off by a factor of ten.

Also, for levels other than level one the probability is higher, by the
fact that levels can have shops with WoW in them. Now computing this requires
the knowledge of probability of generating a shop, average shop size etc
- probably only a Monte-Carlo method has a chance ;-)

